      "remediation": {
        "description": "HTTP API CorsConfiguration sets AllowCredentials to true while AllowOrigins contains \"*\". Browsers will refuse this combination, but the configuration reveals misaligned intent about which origins should be permitted to make credentialed calls.",
        "action": "Either set AllowCredentials to false and keep the wildcard (if the API is genuinely open and cookies/auth headers are not required), or replace the wildcard in AllowOrigins with the explicit set of origins that need credentialed access. Update via \"aws apigatewayv2 update-api --api-id \u003cid\u003e --cors-configuration ...\".",
        "example": "{\n  \"api\": {\n    \"kind\": \"http_api\",\n    \"cors\": {\n      \"configured\": true,\n      \"allows_wildcard_origin\": false,\n      \"credentials_allowed\": true\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
